# Everything the build does not need, and several things it must not have.
#
# `node_modules` above all: the host's tree is built for the host's platform and libc, and copying
# it into the image would shadow the one `pnpm install` just resolved — argon2 is a native module,
# so the failure would be at runtime rather than at build.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. The image builds its own; a stale local `dist` copied in is the E2E stale-build
# trap again, one layer down.
dist
.next
**/dist
**/.next
apps/api/src/generated

# **And the incremental-build state, which is the same trap wearing a smaller hat.** With a host
# `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` copied in, tsc believes the output it describes already exists and emits
# nothing but declarations — so `packages/types/dist` arrived holding three `.d.ts` files and no
# `index.js`, and every import of it failed to resolve. The build was reading a fact about a
# machine it was not running on.
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local state, which must never reach a layer — an image layer is not deletable.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Noise that only invalidates the cache.
.git
.github
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
*.log
.DS_Store
.claude
.docs
docs
